cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProofForge or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "ProofForge: Meta's Muse models as provers of financial code"
abstract: >-
  ProofForge states what financial code must guarantee as locked Lean 4 requirements, refutes code
  that breaks one with a counterexample the Lean kernel checks, and accepts a fix only when six
  independent kernels check its proof. Every verdict is a Passport, bound by hash to the
  specification, the source and the executable, that anyone can re-run. The repository holds the
  judge, the tasks, the ProofForgeFin library, the Muse Code integration and every measured run.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Silva
    given-names: David William
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidwilliam/proof_forge"
url: "https://proofforge.dev"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - smart contract security
  - AI agents
  - Muse Code
